<Shell title="How Origin89 fits your site">
<section class="frame product-page-hero"><div><span class="micro">The Origin89 system / In development</span><h1>Bring the pieces<br />of your site<br />together.</h1><p>A Controller beside the equipment, an app for the owner and help when a reading needs explaining. Each has a clear job.</p><div class="actions"><a class="action" href="/next/equipment/">Find your equipment <span>↗</span></a><a class="text-action" href="/next/sample-site/">See a sample site ↗</a></div></div><Scene /></section>
<section class="frame"><div class="journey-grid"><div><span class="micro">Connect at the site</span><h3>Equipment → Controller</h3><p>Model-specific connections bring readings and supported actions into the system. The Controller runs configured control rules locally.</p></div><div><span class="micro">See what’s happening</span><h3>Controller → Offgrid</h3><p>The app presents the readings, their freshness and your site settings. Remote access depends on connectivity.</p></div><div><span class="micro">Understand the next step</span><h3>Offgrid + Buddy</h3><p>Buddy helps explain readings and proposed settings. You review a proposed change before applying it.</p></div></div></section>
